      "name": "estimated_complexity",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.8,
      "source_groundedness": 0.75,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A complexity tier is a reasonable inferential axis that can help explain and model resolution time. Values are mostly defensible warranted inferences (outage=high, simple enhancement=low). It is inherently subjective but the samples are plausible readings of the text, so groundedness is moderately high."
    },
    {
      "name": "routing_recommendation",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.55,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Routing directly speaks to the query—correct routing reduces resolution time—so it is a useful actionable axis. But it is largely derived from issue_category and inherits its errors: CS-0004 routed to billing specialist (it is a product feature request), and CS-0005 escalated as if an outage. When category is right (auth->security, outage->escalate) routing is sound, but the propagated misreads lower groundedness."
    },
    {
      "name": "self_service_candidate",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.6,
      "source_groundedness": 0.45,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "A binary self-service flag is a plausible lever for reducing ticket load and time, so it has some analytical value, though it is coarser and partly redundant with complexity. Groundedness is weak: CS-0001 (a duplicate-invoice correction needing a human-issued corrected invoice) marked 'yes', and CS-0004 (a product feature request that cannot be self-served) marked 'yes' are poorly supported by the text."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
  "source_groundedness": 0.55,
  "rationale": "The added columns provide genuine new analytical axes (issue type, complexity, routing, self-service) that let an analyst group and model resolution_minutes and identify levers to reduce resolution time—well aligned with the query and not merely redundant with existing columns. However groundedness is only moderate: the visible samples show real misclassifications (feature request tagged billing, export bug tagged outage, an invoice correction and a feature request tagged self-service 'yes'), and these errors propagate into routing_recommendation. The columns are useful in principle but their values are not reliably faithful to the source text."
